    "name": "Spirit Resilience",
    "compareWith": "Bullet Resilience",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obscure",
    "reason": "Spirit Resilience and Bullet Resilience are mirror items with the same price. Players who think of one will usually think of the other, so Spirit Resilience should not sit at 10 while Bullet Resilience sits at 85.",
    "outcome": "applied"
   },
   {
    "name": "Bullet Resilience",
    "compareWith": "Spirit Resilience",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obvious",
    "reason": "Bullet Resilience is a core defensive staple that players buy often, and it is the counterpart of Spirit Resilience at the same price. It is much more recognizable than 85 points implies.",
    "outcome": "applied"
   },
   {
    "name": "Metal Skin",
    "compareWith": "Warp Stone",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obvious",
    "reason": "Metal Skin is a well-known, memorable active that makes you immune to bullets, and players buy it often. It should be about as obvious as Warp Stone, not at 60.",
    "outcome": "applied"
   },
   {
    "name": "Healing Nova",
    "compareWith": "Spirit Snatch",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obvious",
    "reason": "Healing Nova is a common support item that players see and buy often. Its name is clear enough to come to mind before niche melee items like Spirit Snatch.",
    "outcome": "applied"
   },
   {
    "name": "Torment Pulse",
